# Aura connection. Same instance the dashboard and agent read.
NEO4J_URI=neo4j+s://xxxxxxxx.databases.neo4j.io
NEO4J_USERNAME=neo4j
NEO4J_PASSWORD=
NEO4J_DATABASE=neo4j

# Root of instrument output on the share drive.
SOURCE_ROOT=X:\peakFit

# S3, for the raw data (spec.md 5g).
#
# One IAM identity per machine, matching what that machine does. boto3 reads
# exactly one AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID, so the job picks the key - there is nothing to
# rename and no second pair to add:
#
#   runs the backup   ->  cataverse-uploader        PutObject + ListBucket
#   runs the rebuild  ->  cataverse-graph-builder   GetObject + ListBucket
#
# Neither can delete, and neither can do the other's job: a leaked lab-PC key
# cannot read the data back, and a leaked builder key cannot overwrite it.
#
# Record which one this machine holds on the line below. When something returns
# AccessDenied later, that line is the difference between "wrong identity" and
# an hour spent suspecting the key itself.
#
# identity: <cataverse-uploader | cataverse-graph-builder>
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
AWS_REGION=us-east-2
S3_BUCKET=

# If ONE machine runs both jobs - which the lab PC will, once the rebuild is
# scheduled there too - set these instead of the plain pair above. Each command
# then uses its own identity rather than whichever key happened to be in
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID:
#
#   backup            -> UPLOADER_*
#   rebuild, pointers -> BUILDER_*
#
# Worth knowing what this does and does not buy. On two machines the split is
# containment: a leaked lab-PC key cannot read the data back. On one machine it
# is not - whoever has the box has both. What it still gives you is independent
# rotation and, in CloudTrail, which job did what. Both real, neither is
# "an attacker cannot read the bucket".
#
# UPLOADER_AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# UPLOADER_AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# BUILDER_AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# BUILDER_AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=

# Drive holding peakFit, OpusConvert_lgRfl, OpusReadParams, pressureData.
# The backup mirrors everything beneath it.
SHARE_ROOT=X:\
